<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Peter's Basilica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Peter's Basilica is a church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> built over the traditional tomb of the apostle Peter. In the old basilica on this site, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a> crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> emperor on Christmas Day 800 CE. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> treat the coronation as the founding moment of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-peters-basilica.jpg" alt="St. Peter's Basilica" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alvesgaspar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basilica_di_San_Pietro_in_Vaticano_September_2015-1a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
